  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> gas is bubbled through water at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>303</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, the number of millimoles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> gas that dissolve in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> litre of water is____(Nearest integer) (Given : Henry&#39;s Law constant for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>303</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>46</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>82</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math> bar and partial pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>920</mn></math> bar)<br />(Assume solubility of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> in water is too small, nearly negligible)"
  },
